// ⚠⚠ THIS IS THE **TYPECHECK** CONFIG. IT INCLUDES `test`, AND IT DOES NOT BUILD.
//
// `npm run build` uses `tsconfig.build.json`, not this file. The two exist because a
// single config cannot do both jobs here:
//
//   • Typechecking must see `test/`. It did not until 2026-08-16, and that made this
//     the only test directory on the platform no command compiled. A fixture whose
//     literals stopped matching a production type went SILENTLY VACUOUS — vitest
//     strips types without checking them, so the assertions compared against
//     `undefined` and passed. Found only when an unrelated change moved the shape.
//
//   • Emitting must NOT see `test/`. `outDir` is relative to the ROOT DIR, and with
//     `test` in `include` the inferred root moves from `src/` up to `functions/` —
//     measured, not assumed: `lib/index.js` becomes `lib/src/index.js` (breaking
//     `package.json` `main`, and with it the deployed entry point) and 124 compiled
//     test files land in `lib/test/`, inside the bundle Firebase deploys.
//
// ⚠ `rootDir` IS EXPLICIT IN BOTH FILES, and that is the load-bearing part. Left to
// inference it is the common ancestor of the input set, so it moves silently whenever
// `include` changes. Stating it makes the emit a decision instead of a side effect.
//
// This is exactly the layout `packages/game-server` and `packages/stage-engine`
// already use, down to the file names and the script names.
{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "module": "commonjs",
    "noImplicitReturns": true,
    "noUnusedLocals": true,
    "outDir": "lib",
    "rootDir": ".",
    "sourceMap": true,
    "strict": true,
    "target": "es2017",
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true
  },
  "compileOnSave": true,
  "include": [
    "src",
    "test"
  ]
}
